       <div class="col-lg-8">
             <div class="blog-content">
             <img class="blog-hero-image" src="data:image/jpeg;base64," alt="SSC MTS Result 2026: Result Date, Merit List &amp; Cut Off">
             <div class="blog-body">
                <h1 class="blog-title">SSC MTS Result 2026: Your Gateway to Government Service Awaits!</h1>
                <p>The Staff Selection Commission (SSC) Multi-Tasking (Non-Technical) Staff and Havaldar examination is a highly sought-after opportunity for government job aspirants. As we progress into 2026, candidates who appeared for the SSC MTS 2025 cycle examination are eagerly awaiting their results. This comprehensive guide will walk you through the expected result dates, how to access your merit list, understand the cut-off marks, and what comes next in the selection process.</p>

                <h2 class="section-title">SSC MTS 2025 Cycle: Exams Concluded, Results on the Horizon!</h2>
                <p>For those who participated in the SSC MTS / Havaldar Examination 2025, the Computer Based Test (CBT) was held from February 4 to February 15, 2026. The application process for this cycle concluded in July 2025. With the examination now completed, the focus shifts entirely to the result declaration.</p>

                <div class="benefit-card">
                  <p>✅ **Exam Dates (2025 Cycle):** February 4 to February 15, 2026</p>
                  <p>✅ **Expected Result Date (2026):** Typically, results are declared 2-3 months after the examination. Candidates can anticipate the SSC MTS 2025 CBE Paper-I result in April-May 2026.</p>
                </div>

                <h3 class="section-title">How to Check Your SSC MTS Result 2026</h3>
                <p>Once declared, the SSC MTS result will be available on the official SSC website. Follow these steps to access your result:</p>
                <div class="benefit-item">
                  <div class="benefit-title">1. Visit the Official SSC Website</div>
                  <div class="benefit-content">Go to <a href="https://ssc.gov.in" target="_blank">ssc.gov.in</a>. This is the only official portal for result declarations.</div>
                </div>
                <div class="benefit-item">
                  <div class="benefit-title">2. Navigate to the Results Section</div>
                  <div class="benefit-content">On the homepage, click on the 'Results' tab.</div>
                </div>
                <div class="benefit-item">
                  <div class="benefit-title">3. Select the Relevant Exam</div>
                  <div class="benefit-content">Look for the link specifically for "Multi-Tasking (Non-Technical) Staff, and Havaldar (CBIC &amp; CBN) Examination, 2025" or similar.</div>
                </div>
                <div class="benefit-item">
                  <div class="benefit-title">4. Download the Result PDF</div>
                  <div class="benefit-content">The result will be displayed as a PDF file containing the roll numbers of all qualified candidates.</div>
                </div>
                <div class="benefit-item">
                  <div class="benefit-title">5. Search for Your Roll Number</div>
                  <div class="benefit-content">Open the downloaded PDF and use the 'Ctrl + F' function to quickly find your roll number. If your roll number is on the list, congratulations, you have qualified for the next stage!</div>
                </div>
                <div class="benefit-item">
                  <div class="benefit-title">6. Save for Future Reference</div>
                  <div class="benefit-content">It is advisable to download and print a copy of your result for your records.</div>
                </div>

                <h2 class="section-title">Understanding the SSC MTS Merit List</h2>
                <p>The SSC MTS result is released in the form of a merit list, which includes the names and roll numbers of candidates shortlisted for the subsequent stages of the recruitment process. For Multi-Tasking Staff (MTS) posts, final selection is primarily based on Session-II of the Computer-Based Examination. However, candidates for Havaldar posts must also qualify Session-II of the CBE and the Physical Efficiency Test (PET)/Physical Standard Test (PST).</p>
                <p>Along with the merit list, SSC also publishes the category-wise and post-wise cut-off marks.</p>

                <h2 class="section-title">SSC MTS Cut-Off 2026: What to Expect</h2>
                <p>The cut-off marks are the minimum scores required for candidates to qualify for the next stage of the selection process. The SSC MTS cut-off for 2026 (for the 2025 cycle exam) will be released alongside the results. Several factors influence these cut-off marks, including:</p>
                <div class="subsection-paragraph benefit-card">
                  <p>✅ The overall difficulty level of the examination papers.</p>
                  <p>✅ The total number of vacancies available for both MTS and Havaldar posts.</p>
                  <p>✅ The total number of candidates who appeared for the exam.</p>
                  <p>✅ Previous year cut-off trends.</p>
                  <p>✅ The average marks obtained by candidates.</p>
                </div>

                <p>SSC releases the cut-off marks state/UT-wise and category-wise (UR, OBC, SC, ST, EWS, ESM). While the exact cut-off for 2026 will only be known upon official release, candidates should be aware of the minimum qualifying marks for the Computer Based Test (CBT):</p>
                <div class="highlight-text">
                  <ul>
                    <li>General Category: 30%</li>
                    <li>EWS / OBC Category: 25%</li>
                    <li>Other Reserved Categories: 20%</li>
                  </ul>
                  <p>These are minimum passing marks, and the actual cut-off will likely be higher, especially for competitive states and categories.</p>
                </div>
                <p>For a strategic understanding, reviewing previous years' cut-off marks can provide valuable insights into competition levels and expected scores. These are typically available on the official SSC website.</p>

                <h2 class="section-title">What Happens After the SSC MTS Result?</h2>
                <p>Qualifying the CBT is a significant step, but it's not the final one for all candidates.</p>
                <div class="benefit-item">
                  <div class="benefit-title">1. Document Verification (DV)</div>
                  <div class="benefit-content">All shortlisted candidates will be called for Document Verification. This stage usually takes about 3-4 weeks after the result declaration. Candidates must present original documents such as educational certificates (10th pass), identity proofs, and category certificates (if applicable).</div>
                </div>
                <div class="benefit-item">
                  <div class="benefit-title">2. Physical Efficiency Test (PET) / Physical Standard Test (PST)</div>
                  <div class="benefit-content">This stage is mandatory only for candidates who applied for Havaldar posts. It involves specific physical requirements like walking and cycling tests, along with height and chest measurements. Those who clear the PET/PST will proceed to a Medical Examination.</div>
                </div>
                <div class="benefit-item">
                  <div class="benefit-title">3. Final Merit List</div>
                  <div class="benefit-content">A final merit list will be prepared after all stages are completed. This list determines the final selection of candidates for the Multi-Tasking Staff and Havaldar positions. SSC does not maintain a waiting list.</div>
                </div>

                <h2 class="section-title">Looking Ahead: SSC MTS 2026 Notification &amp; Exam</h2>
                <p>For those aspiring to appear in future cycles, the SSC MTS 2026 notification is expected to be released in June 2026. The online application process would likely run through July 2026, with the Computer Based Test (CBT) tentatively scheduled between September and November 2026. Keep a close watch on the official SSC website for these important announcements.</p>

                <p>We wish all candidates the very best for their SSC MTS Result 2026! Remember to regularly check the official Staff Selection Commission website for the most accurate and up-to-date information regarding your results and the further selection process.</p>
             </div>
             </div>
       </div>

            
